        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-11T14:26:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you\u0027d be better off with a design like the following :\n\n  @Nonnull\n  private final T mResource;\n  @NonNull\n  private final List\u003cRefcountedResource\u003e mChildren;\n  @Nullable\n  IBinder mBinder;\n\n  RefcountedResource(@NonNull T resource, @Nullable IBinder binder, @NonNull RefcountedResource... children) {\n  ...\n  }\n\n  RefcountedResource(@NonNull T resource, @NonNull RefcountedResource... children) {\n    this(resource, null, children);\n  }\n\n\nI think this is much more idiomatic Java, and gives you some guarantees about nullability.",
      "range": {
