    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "afd153fa_33819704",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/IpSecService.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 254,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-11T14:26:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So let me get this straight :\nThis is a reference counted resource that increments their refcount by being added to a parent, and decrements them when a parent is fully released. But it can also be released by the user, and *that\u0027s* when it frees its resources. Well some of them, the ones in invalidate().\n\nIs there any way to make this simpler and closer to what we usually call a \"reference counted\" object ? Or to rename it to better reflect what it is ?\n(not for this patch obviously)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 254,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 254,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "c99ea44577aa0c6763f7f34e05affe6069a24162",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e505b2d_2bad92e6",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/IpSecService.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 254,
      "author": {
        "id": 1221725
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-03T14:33:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Almost; both conditions must be triggered in order to free it\u0027s resources (and they have equal priority):\n1. User must have called close(), or binder must have died\n2. All dependent resources must release their reference on \"this\" resource.\n\nInvalidate() makes sure the resource is no longer accessible to the user once it has been closed. No resource cleanup actually occurs there.\n\nOn the other hand, the freeUnderlyingResources() (called from releaseReference()) will perform the actual cleanup.\n\nBut at a higher level, I\u0027m not sure how much we could simplify this. The primary motivation for doing this was to guarantee a specific cleanup ordering between resources, while also making sure that any references that a user has would be valid while they hold them. If you\u0027re curious, the design doc was go/ipsecservice-resource-management. \n\nRegarding naming, I think we settled on these names after changing it four times, so i\u0027m somewhat hesitant to change it again :)",
      "parentUuid": "afd153fa_33819704",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 254,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 254,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "c99ea44577aa0c6763f7f34e05affe6069a24162",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
