      "writtenOn": "2019-03-11T14:26:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems to me like it flies in the face of the contract for OwnedResourceRecord AND the comment in 1022. A ResourceTracker object is just a glorified semaphore (sans the thread-safety :/), why not make one and initialize it to the rlimit for FDs or something ?\n\nI do find it dangerous to say hey, this method that used to never return null, well now it can",
